  "comment": "The four UK nations for the globe's zoomed-in layer — companion config to us-states.json, consumed by scripts/build-state-data.mjs --region uk. `query` lists the MusicBrainz area names swept during precompute (nation name + curated music cities/scenes). Names shared with other countries (Bangor, Newport, Boston, Birmingham…) are swept once and every hit is assigned to its true nation by walking the area's parents to a GB-ENG/SCT/WLS/NIR ISO code, so collisions cost recall pages, never accuracy. UK cities carry their OWN ISO-3166-2 codes (Manchester GB-MAN, Glasgow GB-GLG) — the walk continues through non-target subdivision codes and stops only at country codes. `aliases` are extra search-box spellings. `pages` overrides per-name sweep depth for known-huge areas.",
